[
    {
        "content": "<p>Looking at loogle, I don't for instance see any joint mention of <code>RelHom</code> with <code>TransGen</code>. But we have some theorems like <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Relation.TransGen.lift#doc\">docs#Relation.TransGen.lift</a> that are naturally phrased this way, e.g.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Relation</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- naming???</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RelHom</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TransGen</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TransGen</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TransGen</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TransGen</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lift</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map_rel'</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I'd ask if this should be the way to state these theorems, but there is a wrinkle with universes. Should these then at least be additionally added to Mathlib?</p>",
        "id": 604120971,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1781696687
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(though there's been some back and forth about reverting <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/34391\">#34391</a>. I agree with matching the generality of core in principle but it makes things like this mildly awkward. )</p>",
        "id": 604128570,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1781698238
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Tangentially: Arguably that should be called <code>map</code>, and <code>lift</code> should be used for creating a map <del>out of</del> into an arbitrary transitive relation (which is presumably only the same up to propeq/funext), as <code>TransGen r</code> is of course the smallest transitive relation larger than <code>r</code></p>",
        "id": 604130813,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1781698673
    }
]